From a71495a10a3c03df86f46d723f82e62774ddd674 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Giacone <giaconejoshua@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 14:51:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] add MpcLeadTrajectory dev-menu toggle for model-predicted
 lead trajectory

Ports commaai/openpilot#37824 (draft, "long mpc: use model predicted lead
trajectory") as an opt-in toggle instead of a blanket replacement, following
the same pattern as SPLC (LaneCentering param + toggle_item_sp/BigParamControl
in both developer-menu layouts).

When off (default): unchanged legacy kinematic lead extrapolation from radar
state (process_lead_legacy), CRUISE_MAX_ACCEL stays 1.6.

When on: MPC plans against the driving model's full predicted lead trajectory
(0-10s, leadsV3) anchored to the radar's h=0 measurement, letting it react
earlier to a lead braking hard for a stop and ignore brief spurious slowdowns.
Pairs with a higher CRUISE_MAX_ACCEL_MODEL_LEAD (2.0) since the smarter lead
sensing affords a snappier response. Toggle state is polled on the same
PARAMS_UPDATE_PERIOD cadence sunnypilot uses elsewhere for realtime params.

Adds leadTrajectoryX0/V0/X1/V1 to LongitudinalPlan for logging/debugging
regardless of toggle state.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
